# HTTPS in front of Food-Assistant (ADR-0007). Caddy gets and renews the certificate itself
# (Let's Encrypt); the domain must point to this machine and ports 80/443 must be reachable.
# Caddy sends X-Forwarded-For/-Proto; the server trusts them from the Docker network.
#
# No `encode` here: it changes the ETags of compressed API responses ("42" -> "42-zstd"), and
# If-Match with such a tag would never match (ADR-0004). Static web-app files are served
# precompressed by the server anyway.

{$FOODASSISTANT_DOMAIN} {
    reverse_proxy server:8080
}
